.TH WAYPARAM 1 "September 2026" "wayparam 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayparam \- fetch and normalize parameterized URLs from public web archive indexes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayparam
.RI [ options ] " -d DOMAIN"
.br
.B wayparam
.RI [ options ] " -l FILE"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayparam
queries public web archive indexes to retrieve historical URLs for a host
(or a list of hosts), filters out common static/boring URLs, and outputs normalized URLs
that contain query parameters. Wayback is the default source; Common Crawl can be
selected alone or combined with Wayback.

By default, query parameter values are replaced with a placeholder (default:
.BR FUZZ ),
making the output suitable for sharing and fuzzing workflows.

The tool is intended for OSINT-style URL collection. It does not crawl targets; it queries
archive indexes only.
.SH OUTPUT BEHAVIOR
Diagnostics (logs, hints, stats) are written to
.BR stderr .
Machine-readable results (URLs or JSONL) are written to
.BR stdout
only when
.BR --stdout
is set.

Per-domain files are written to
.BR results/
by default, unless
.BR --no-files
is specified.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR
Query a single domain/host (e.g.
.IR example.com ).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list " " \fIFILE\fR
Read domains/hosts from a file (one per line). Use
.B \-
to read from stdin.
.SS Archive Sources
.TP
.BR \-\-source " " \fINAME[,NAME...]\fR
Archive provider(s) in priority order. Supported values are
.B wayback
and
.B commoncrawl
(default:
.BR wayback ).
Normalized URLs are deduplicated across providers.
.TP
.BR \-\-provenance
Preserve one normalized record per archive source instead of globally
deduplicating the same endpoint across selected providers. This mode requires
.BR "--format jsonl"
because text output cannot represent source provenance. Repeated variants within
the same source are still deduplicated.
.TP
.BR \-\-cc\-index " " \fIID\fR
Common Crawl crawl index ID. Repeat or use comma-separated IDs to query several
collections. The default is
.BR latest ,
resolved from Common Crawl collection metadata.
.TP
.BR \-\-cc\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Compressed Common Crawl ZipNum index blocks per page (default: 5). This is not a
row count.
.TP
.BR \-\-cc\-rps " " \fIFLOAT\fR
Common Crawl index requests per second (default: 1). Requests to Common Crawl
are also serialized within a run.
.TP
.BR \-\-cc\-filter " " \fIFILTER\fR
Add a Common Crawl CDXJ filter (repeatable), for example
.IR status:200 .
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-outdir " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory for per-domain result files (default:
.IR results ).
.TP
.BR \-\-stdout
Stream results to stdout (machine-readable). Diagnostics remain on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " {txt|jsonl}
Output format for stdout and per-domain files (default:
.IR txt ).
.RS
.TP
.B txt
One URL per line.
.TP
.B jsonl
JSON Lines records with keys:
.BR domain ,
.BR url ,
.BR source ,
.BR fetched_at .
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-files
Do not write per-domain output files. Requires
.BR --stdout .
.TP
.BR \-\-stats
Print per-domain counts (fetched/kept) to stderr at the end.
.TP
.BR \-\-history
Aggregate uncollapsed capture metadata per normalized URL. Records include first
and last seen timestamps, capture counts, status-code counts and MIME-type
counts. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-params
and
.BR \-\-summary .
.TP
.BR \-\-params
Aggregate historical prevalence by query-parameter name, including endpoint
count, represented captures and first/last seen timestamps.
.TP
.BR \-\-summary
Emit one historical aggregate record per domain.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeline
Aggregate accepted historical archive evidence into time buckets. Each record
reports captures, observed and newly seen normalized URLs, and observed and
newly seen query-parameter names.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeline\-granularity " " \fIyear|month\fR
Choose the bucket size used by
.BR \-\-timeline
(default:
.BR year ).
.TP
.BR \-\-changes " " \fIBASELINE COMPARISON\fR
Compare archive evidence between two periods. Both values must use the same
granularity, either YYYY or YYYYMM, and BASELINE must be earlier than
COMPARISON. Output classifies normalized URLs and parameter names as added,
removed or persisted. These classifications describe archive evidence, not
current live-target state.
.TP
.BR \-\-source\-summary
Compare normalized URL coverage across at least two selected archive sources.
The summary reports the union, per-source counts, source-exclusive counts, URLs
shared by at least two sources, and the intersection observed by every selected
source. Output files use
.IR <domain>.sources.{txt,jsonl} .
.PP
Historical modes currently require
.BR "--source wayback" .
They automatically disable Wayback CDX collapse so capture counts and
first/last-seen dates are meaningful. This may transfer substantially more data
than a normal URL run.
.SS Shared Archive Query
.TP
.BR \-\-include\-subdomains
Include subdomains by using CDX matchType=domain (default: host only).
.TP
.BR \-\-from " " \fITIMESTAMP\fR
Only include captures from this timestamp/year (e.g.
.IR 2019
or
.IR 20190101000000 ).
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fITIMESTAMP\fR
Only include captures up to this timestamp/year.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-collapse
Disable archive-index collapse=urlkey (returns more duplicates and more data).
.SS Wayback / CDX
.TP
.BR \-\-pagination " " \fIauto|blocks|resume\fR
How to walk a result that does not fit in one response (default: auto). The CDX
API offers two mechanisms: resumeKey paging, whose cost follows the size of the
filtered result but which drops one row at each page boundary while collapse is
on, and block paging (showNumPages/page), which is lossless but whose cost
follows the size of the domain's index.
.B auto
sends one resumeKey request and stops there if the whole result arrived -- a
single response has no boundary to lose anything at -- and otherwise restarts
through the block API.
.TP
.BR \-\-block\-size " " \fIN\fR
CDX index blocks per request in block mode (default: 100). Larger means fewer
but slower and heavier responses.
.TP
.BR \-\-filter " " \fIFILTER\fR
Add a Wayback CDX filter string (repeatable). Example:
.IR statuscode:200 .
.TP
.BR \-\-limit ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Aliases. CDX rows per request in resumeKey mode. This is a page size, not a cap on
results (default: 50000). See
.BR \-\-max\-results
to bound a run.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-results " " \fIN\fR
Stop the whole run after this many URLs. The budget is global, shared by every
domain in the run (default: 0, no cap). In historical analysis modes the budget
counts accepted capture rows before aggregation. In source-summary mode the
same cap is applied independently to each selected archive source, so an
earlier provider cannot consume the entire comparison budget. A bounded source
summary is marked incomplete. A run stopped by the budget exits 0, and
.BR \-\-stats
marks the affected domains as incomplete.
.SS Normalization and Filtering
.TP
.BR \-\-placeholder " " \fISTR\fR
Placeholder used for query parameter values (default:
.IR FUZZ ).
.TP
.BR \-\-keep\-values
Keep original query parameter values (not recommended for sharing logs).
.TP
.BR \-\-all\-urls
Include URLs without query parameters (default: only URLs with parameters).
.TP
.BR \-\-drop\-tracking " / " \-\-no\-drop\-tracking
Drop or keep common tracking parameters (default: drop).
.TP
.BR \-\-ext\-blacklist " " \fICSV\fR
Comma-separated list of extensions to exclude (overrides defaults), e.g.
.IR ".png,.jpg,.css" .
.TP
.BR \-\-ext\-whitelist " " \fICSV\fR
Comma-separated list of extensions to allow; anything else is excluded. A
whitelist replaces the blacklist rather than being narrowed by it. Paths with no
extension are not judged by extension and pass either way.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-path\-regex " " \fIREGEX\fR
Regex to exclude URLs by path (repeatable).
.SS Performance and Network
.TP
.BR \-\-concurrency " " \fIN\fR
Number of domains processed concurrently (default: 6).
.TP
.BR \-\-rps " " \fIFLOAT\fR
Global requests per second to the Wayback CDX API (default: 0 = unlimited).
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
HTTP timeout in seconds (default: 30).
.TP
.BR \-\-retries " " \fIN\fR
HTTP retry attempts (default: 4).
.TP
.BR \-\-proxy " " \fIURL\fR
HTTP proxy URL (e.g.
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8080 ).
When Common Crawl is selected, wayparam warns because its public-index guidance
advises against proxy networks.
.TP
.BR \-\-user\-agent " " \fISTR\fR
Override the User-Agent header.
.TP
.BR \-\-quiet
Only show errors (stderr).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-vv
Increase verbosity (stderr).
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch URLs for a single domain and write results to
.IR results/example.com.txt :
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream URLs to stdout (for piping) and do not write files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --stdout --no-files
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write JSONL output and print stats to stderr:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -l domains.txt --format jsonl --stats
.fi
.RE
.PP
Be polite to the Wayback API:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --rps 1 --concurrency 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query the latest Common Crawl index:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --source commoncrawl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Combine Wayback and Common Crawl, deduplicating in that order:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --source wayback,commoncrawl --format jsonl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compare normalized URL coverage between Wayback and Common Crawl:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --source wayback,commoncrawl --source-summary --format jsonl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit historical endpoint metadata as JSONL:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --history --stdout --no-files --format jsonl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Summarize historical parameter prevalence:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --params
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build a month-by-month archive timeline:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --timeline --timeline-granularity month --format jsonl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compare archive evidence between two years:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wayparam -d example.com --changes 2020 2024 --format jsonl
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I results/<domain>.txt
Default per-domain output file (txt format).
.TP
.I results/<domain>.jsonl
Per-domain output file when using
.BR --format jsonl .
.TP
.I results/<domain>.history.{txt,jsonl}
Historical endpoint analysis.
.TP
.I results/<domain>.params.{txt,jsonl}
Historical parameter analysis.
.TP
.I results/<domain>.summary.{txt,jsonl}
Historical domain summary.
.TP
.I results/<domain>.timeline.{txt,jsonl}
Historical temporal timeline.
.TP
.I results/<domain>.changes.{txt,jsonl}
Historical comparison between two archive periods.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (all domains processed).
.TP
.B 2
Partial failure (one or more domains failed).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by user (Ctrl+C).
.TP
.B 141
Output pipe closed by the consumer (for example
.BR "wayparam -d example.com --stdout | head" ).
This is normal in pipelines and is reported quietly.
.SH NOTES
If Wayback requests consistently fail after retries, a VPN/proxy exit node may
be blocked or rate-limited by
.IR web.archive.org .
Common Crawl's public index is also rate-limited; wayparam serializes those
requests and defaults to one request per second.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR jq (1)
